    "totalDuration": "13 yrs 2 mos",
    "description": "Microsoft Corporation, Windows Division\n1. Win8: Architected and successfully implemented a new print platform for the next generation of Windows development platform -- WWA (Windows web application platform). Single-handedly designed the print platform and integrated it to IE10. Defined and implemented the API set to support developer consumption. Successfully implemented a complete end- to- end solution that enable great print experience for WWAs. The whole feature is rated one of the most important pillar scenarios for Win8.\n\n2. Win8: Made significant contribution to the modern print architecture for Win8. Defined and implemented the Win8 print preview architecture.  \n\n3. Win7: Architected and implemented the Windows Device & Printers and printer device stage. Successfully implemented print components to support the Device and Printers. The whole feature was rated the most innovative device feature in Win7. \n\n4. Win7: Successfully implemented location aware printer and multiple other features. Location aware printer was rated highly for Win7 release. Received patents for creative ideas related to these features.\n\n5. Vista: Designed a multithreaded and lock free cache to support all print device UIs (including device center in Win7). Made huge performance improvement for the Print Management Console – Microsoft’s premier enterprise print management toolset with the cache -- load capacity went from around 10 print servers to over 1000 print servers. Load time improved 1000%. Column sorting time improved more than 500%...\n\n6. Window server 2003 R2 release. Single-handedly designed and implemented Print Management Console – Microsoft’s premier enterprise grade print management solution. This product was rated one of the most innovative product in the release. It is then shipped with Vista and Win7 as a standard OS component.  \n",
